  "worked_solution": "We substitute the given value into each of the inequalities and check to see if the resulting statement is true or false.\n\n- We substitute the value $y=-1$ into the first inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2<y+1 & <8 \\\\ 2<-1+1 & <8 \\\\ 2<0 & <8\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $y=-1$ leads to a **false** statement. \n\nTherefore, $y=-1$ ** does not satisfy** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $y=-1$ into the second inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y & <5 \\\\ 4\\cdot (-1) & <5 \\\\ -4 & <5\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $y=-1$ leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $y=-1$ **satisfies** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $y=-1$ into the third inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & \\le y+3 \\\\ 2 & \\le -1+3 \\\\ 2 & \\le 2\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $y=-1$ leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $y=-1$ **satisfies** this inequality.",
